title: How the shell runs a command
round start: you press Enter
box read: the shell reads the line and splits it into words
diamond q: built in?
box run: run it inside the shell
box fork: `fork()` a child\nprocess
box exec: child calls `exec()`
box wait: shell waits for the child to finish
round done: prompt again
start -> read -> q
q -> run: yes
q -> fork: no
fork -> exec
fork ..> wait: parent
exec -> done
run -> done
wait -> read: next line
